  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 246 PM CDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nWarm and humid conditions continue through Friday before a pattern \nchange starts to take place. The 500mb ridge that Iowa sits on the \nperiphery on begins to shrink and move to the west. Temperatures \nthrough most of the long-term will be cooler, with highs generally \nin the 80s and overnight lows falling into the 60s across much of \nthe state. The long term looks to be fairly dry as well. There are \nsome lower thunderstorm chances Wednesday night into Thursday as a \nshortwave is expected to ride overtop of the ridge. Most of the \nactivity should be out west in Nebraska. The placement of the \nshortwave as it moves through will be better assessed tomorrow and \nWednesday. Thursday night, a low develops over the Dakotas and will \nmove to the east. This low will drive higher shower and thunderstorm \nchances as it moves through, bringing with it a cold front, leading \nto much lower temperatures than we've seen to start the weekend.",
